# Environment of the launchway-runner service. Readable by root only: systemd reads it before
# starting the runner as the launchway-runner user. Steps never see these variables.
#
# The runner token (or a runner pool's token), from the server's administrator.
LAUNCHWAY_RUNNER_TOKEN=
#
# A proxy for the runner's connections to the server and for Git. Long polls last 25 seconds, so
# a proxy's idle timeout must be longer than 30 seconds.
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example.com:3128
# HTTP_PROXY=http://proxy.example.com:3128
# NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1,.internal.example.com
#
# A CA bundle to trust instead of the system's, for a server behind a private CA or a proxy that
# inspects TLS. It must also hold the public CAs you need. install.sh --ca-file writes one.
# SSL_CERT_FILE=/etc/launchway/ca-bundle.pem
# GIT_SSL_CAINFO=/etc/launchway/ca-bundle.pem
